content:
Rejection is the second way in which a claim under `Cargo Liability, CargoCare and Cargo Claims` can be decided, the other being approval for settlement. Every rejection carries one reason taken from a controlled list.

## Rejections that follow registration at once

This reference also covers the decision, taken on a notice once it is on file, whether it is rejected at once on grounds that depend on nothing beyond three records (the cover, the notice, and the refrigerated service attached to the container that the notice names), and if so with which controlled reason. A notice to which none of those grounds applies is not rejected on them.

## Capability of the tool

`reject_cargo_claim_5f9631bd` decides a single cargo claim against the claimant. Each call adds a rejection entry for the claim, at 0.00 USD and with today's date, to the premium and settlement record of the cover; the entry states the controlled reason and names the file's claimant. The claim file's outcome becomes rejected. The cover's status is left alone.

## Invocation

The desk agent operates this tool itself: it is unlocked by the agent and then called by the agent with the three values below.

## Parameters

- `cover_id`: the cover under which the claim was lodged, taken from the cover lookup or the claim-file lookup. Identifier.
- `claim_id`: the claim file to be rejected, taken from the claim-file lookup or from the reference the lodging produced. Identifier.
- `rejection_reason`: the controlled reason, exactly one of:
  - `notice_out_of_time`: the written notice arrived later than the notice window allowed for its kind of loss;
  - `claim_time_barred`: the notice arrived once the claim time bar had passed;
  - `excluded_peril`: the survey put the loss down to the claimant's own inadequate packing or to inherent vice;
  - `not_covered_by_tier`: the tier does not pay this kind of loss, or the loss is temperature damage on a container whose reefer service ranks below the tier's minimum;
  - `no_logged_excursion`: a temperature claim lacks the logged excursion its tier demands;
  - `misdeclared_cargo`: a misdeclaration penalty stands on the dangerous-goods acceptance for the goods;
  - `below_minimum_claim`: the amount falls short of the tier's minimum claim;
  - `documents_not_submitted`: the documents deadline has gone by with the documents still incomplete;
  - `claimant_not_entitled`: the claimant is not the cover holder and not a named consignee the tier admits;
  - `not_applicable`: never right for a rejection; reserved for other entries.

## Return

When the rejection is booked, the tool reports `status` "rejected", `rejection_event_id` identifying the entry just booked, `claim_id`, `cover_id`, `rejection_reason` as recorded, and `amount_usd`, which on a rejection is always 0.00. The claimant may then be informed of the rejection reference and of the reason recorded.
